[Q13] numeric proof of the head->kv mapping
      repeat_kv(kv where kvhead0=1, kvhead1=2, groups=4).reshape(-1)[per head] = [1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 2.0, 2.0, 2.0, 2.0]
      => head h uses kv head  floor(h / groups) = [0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1]
      (NOT h % nkv  -> [0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1] )

[Q11] cos used by apply_rotary_pos_emb (full-tensor case): rotary_dim = cos.shape[-1]
      cos handed to apply_rotary_pos_emb is the WHOLE tensor of last-dim 64
      -> rotary_dim = 64, q_rot = q[..., :64], q_pass = q[..., 64:256], so 192 dims pass through
      (In exp_rotary's earlier calls I sliced cos to 64 manually; both give the same result
       because cos[..., :64] == cos[..., 64:] for this duplicated layout.)
